## THE TICKETS (written verbatim here; `<<...>>` filled by program at Steps 2 and 5; one line = one summary or one ADF paragraph; no card id, no person)
BEGIN <TICKET-SUMMARY-1>
[B1343-1] ApiFactoryHostStartRetryTests: on SQLite the row's assertion that no session was killed cannot fail, because the kill counter is passed to no SQLite host (Minor, test-only)
END <TICKET-SUMMARY-1>
BEGIN <TICKET-DESCRIPTION-1>
BLUF: the new row that starts two hosts together on one fresh database after a lost migrations lock asserts, on its SQLite branch, that no session was killed, and that assertion cannot fail: the counter it reads is handed to no SQLite host. It changes no product behaviour, the file passes on SQLite, and nothing here is deployed. This is finding B1343-1 of gate B1343 (Minor, test-only).
Finding B1343-1: at main <<MAIN-SHA8>> the row Two_hosts_starting_together_on_one_fresh_database_both_start_when_one_loses_its_migrations_lock_session in api/tests/HpsmPoc.Api.Tests/Hosting/ApiFactoryHostStartRetryTests.cs builds the kill counter kills at line <<L-KILLS>>; lines <<L-HOSTS>> give it to the hosts only when the run is on SQL Server (on SQLite the hosts get the wait alone); and on SQLite the row asserts Assert.Empty(kills.Killed) at line <<L-ASSERT>>. Nothing on the SQLite path can add to kills, so the assertion cannot fail. The SQLite half's real content is Assert.Empty(retries) at line <<L-RETRIES>> and the per-host health and pending-migration checks. Read on <<READ-DATE>> by program: the word kills occurs at lines <<L-USES>>.
How it was found: gate B1343 (round 1 of 2, GO WITH FINDINGS) read the file; its instrument was grep -n -w kills over the head (its STATUS 1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-06_B1343_STATUS.md line <<L-F1>>). The row landed as pull request 293 (squash eaf77b3c, merged 2026-11-06 19:21:10 AEDT); the builder's note is B1326.
Evidence, the gate's and not re-run by the records seat: the file passes on SQLite 50 of 50, three times, so the line does no harm; on a real SQL Server the assertions on kills are live (the kill reaches only the row's own session, the gate measured). The records seat re-read the lines above by program and ran no test.
Fix shape, as the gate wrote it, offered as a proposal and not a decision: delete the line, or attach a counting interceptor to the SQLite hosts and assert on that. Which of the two, if either, is wanted is open.
Done when: the line at <<L-ASSERT>> is removed, or the SQLite hosts count their kills and the assertion turns red under a plant that makes one host kill; or the item is recorded as accepted or declined; the SQL Server half of the row is unchanged; no product behaviour changes. Provenance: gate B1343 finding B1343-1 (1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-06_B1343_STATUS.md line <<L-F1>>), builder note B1326, pull request 293; decision records: entry <<C2>> and backlog row B1349-2. Filed by records brief B1349, 2026-11-06. [REC-FILE-B1343-1-06NOV-B1349]
END <TICKET-DESCRIPTION-1>
BEGIN <TICKET-SUMMARY-4>
[B1343-4] Api test-host start retry: a session lost before EF's migration proper (SqlClient: connection broken, no recovery) is not retried; Support/HostStartRetry.cs matches error 1223 on the migrations lock only (Note, test support)
END <TICKET-SUMMARY-4>
BEGIN <TICKET-DESCRIPTION-4>
BLUF: the retry that starts a test host again after a lost EF migrations lock matches one failure only, SQL Server error 1223 whose message names the migrations lock. If the server loses the lock holder's session earlier, before EF's migration proper, the start fails with a different SqlClient error and is not retried. The row added for HPSMPOC-308 does not claim that window. It changes no product behaviour (test support only), whether CI's real session losses fall in that window is not known, and nothing here is deployed. This is finding B1343-4 of gate B1343 (a Note), which the builder of the row also disclosed.
Finding B1343-4: at main <<MAIN-SHA8>> api/tests/HpsmPoc.Api.Tests/Support/HostStartRetry.cs line <<L-FILTER>> accepts a SqlException whose Number is the lock-not-held constant and whose message contains the migrations lock name, and nothing else. The Feedback project's copy (api/tests/HpsmPoc.Modules.Feedback.Tests/Support/HostStartRetry.cs, filter at line <<L-FB>>) is the same code: a diff of the two files at main prints <<N-DIFF>> lines, the header comment and the namespace. Killing the lock holder right after the grant, inside EF's first strategy block, makes the start fail with a SqlClient message that the connection is broken and recovery is not possible, which the filter does not match. Read on <<READ-DATE>> by program.
How it was found: gate B1343 (round 1 of 2, GO WITH FINDINGS), plant Y3, 10 of 10 red with that message (its STATUS 1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-06_B1343_STATUS.md line <<L-F4>>); the builder saw it first, 5 of 5, on a real SQL Server (B1326 line <<L-B1326-119>>). The row landed as pull request 293 (squash eaf77b3c).
Evidence, the gate's and the builder's, not re-run by the records seat: a real SQL Server 2025 container, the lock holder's session killed right after the grant; the unforced shape never produced the fault in 60 of the gate's repeats and 90 of the builder's, so how often CI loses a session at all is unmeasured.
Fix shape, offered as a proposal and not a decision: the gate left open whether this deserves a wider filter or no change. (a) A wider filter in both copies that also accepts the unrecoverable-connection failure, with a row that forces that loss on a real SQL Server and is red without the widening. (b) No change, with the gap stated in the file's header. The gate named only the wider filter; option (b) completes the choice and is this record's own.
Done when: either the filter in both copies also covers a session lost before EF's migration proper, with a row that forces that loss and is red without the change; or the gap is recorded as accepted or declined, with its reason, and the file header says which windows the filter covers; no product behaviour changes. Provenance: gate B1343 finding B1343-4 (1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-06_B1343_STATUS.md line <<L-F4>>), builder note B1326 line <<L-B1326-119>>, pull request 293; decision records: entry <<C2>> and backlog row B1349-2. Filed by records brief B1349, 2026-11-06. [REC-FILE-B1343-4-06NOV-B1349]
END <TICKET-DESCRIPTION-4>
(Six paragraphs each, one per line of the description block. `<<L-USES>>` is the lines printed by `grep -n -w kills`, joined by commas and "and"; `<<N-DIFF>>` is the number of differing lines `diff` printed (expected 3); `<<L-F1>>` and `<<L-F4>>` are the lines of the gate's STATUS that begin `- **B1343-1` and `- **B1343-4` (expected 130 and 133); `<<L-B1326-119>>` the line of the builder's STATUS that begins `- **Seen outside scope:**` (expected 119). The longest paragraph is under 3000 characters: print each length. Each text is under the limit of Jira's description field; assert it.)

